§9  SAEIS ENFORCEMENT ARCHITECTURE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  SAEIS — Sovereign AI Enforcement & Integrity System

  Enforcement Layers:
  ────────────────────

  Layer 1: PROCESS LEVEL
    └── Every ANIMA Runtime process binds a SAT token at spawn
    └── Token = SAT-ANIMA-{PID}-{TIMESTAMP}
    └── No process executes without valid SAT binding

  Layer 2: MODULE LEVEL
    └── Every import/require passes through SAEIS validation
    └── Module integrity verified against sovereign registry hashes
    └── Unauthorized modules rejected at load time

  Layer 3: PACKAGE LEVEL
    └── FORMA model validates all packages before registry publish
    └── ISIL-1.1 compliance checked on every package version
    └── Cross-ecosystem translations validated by LEXIS model

  Layer 4: REGISTRY LEVEL
    └── Both MEDINA PKG and SOVEREIGN REGISTRY enforce SAEIS
    └── Package provenance tracking across all 6 ecosystems
    └── Container image signing and verification

  Layer 5: NETWORK LEVEL
    └── Nova sovereign encryption on all registry communications
    └── Quantum-resistant key exchange for sovereign packages
    └── Inter-organism resonance authenticated via φ-signatures


