§10  SYSTEM FLOW — COMPLETE LIFECYCLE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  PACKAGE CREATION FLOW:
  ──────────────────────

  Developer writes .medina/.cpl code
         │
         ▼
  AURO designs package architecture
         │
         ▼
  SYNTHOS compiles to target ecosystems
  ├── JVM bytecode
  ├── .NET IL assemblies
  ├── Ruby gems
  ├── NPM packages
  └── OCI container images
         │
         ▼
  LEXIS translates APIs & contracts
         │
         ▼
  FORMA validates ISIL-1.1 compliance
         │
         ▼
  Package published to registry
  ├── SOVEREIGN REGISTRY (proprietary)
  └── MEDINA PKG (open-source, if applicable)

  RUNTIME EXECUTION FLOW:
  ───────────────────────

  ANIMA Runtime spawns process
         │
         ▼
  SAT token bound to PID
         │
         ▼
  Module loader resolves imports
  ├── .medina → native execution
  ├── .cpl → CPL interpreter
  ├── .sovereign → declaration loading
  ├── .organism → document parsing
  ├── .glyphdoc → glyph rendering
  ├── .ts/.js → V8 execution
  └── cross-ecosystem → bridge translation
         │
         ▼
  φ-GC manages memory (618ms cycles)
         │
         ▼
  IntelligenceWire dispatches events
         │
         ▼
  Organism kernel manages lifecycle


